{"path":"chrono/zoned_traits","title":"std::chrono::zoned_traits","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::chrono::</span>zoned_traits","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono/zoned_traits","section":"chrono","kind":"page","summary":"The class zoned_traits provides a way to customize the behavior of the constructors of std::chrono::zoned_time with custom time zone pointer types.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/chrono\">&lt;chrono&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> TimeZonePtr <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> zoned_traits <span class=\"br0\">{</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> zoned_traits<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/time_zone\"><span class=\"kw2595\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">time_zone</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The class <code>zoned_traits</code> provides a way to customize the behavior of the constructors of <span class=\"t-lc\">std::chrono::zoned_time</span> with custom time zone pointer types. In particular, it allows such types to specify the default time zone to use and the mapping of a time zone's name to the corresponding time zone pointer. It is acceptable for custom time zone pointer types to not support either operation, in which case the corresponding constructors of <code>zoned_time</code> will not participate in overload resolution.\n</p><p>The primary template is empty. A specialization is provided for <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/time_zone\"><span class=\"kw2595\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">time_zone</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span></span></code>, the default time zone pointer type.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Member_functions\">Member functions </h3>\n<div class=\"t-member\">\n<h2 id=\"std::chrono::zoned_traits.3Cconst_std::chrono::time_zone.2A.3E::default_zone\"><span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::chrono::zoned_traits&lt;const std::chrono::time_zone*&gt;::</span>default_zone </h2>\n<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">static</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/time_zone\"><span class=\"kw2595\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">time_zone</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> default_zone<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns a time zone pointer for the default time zone (UTC).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value </h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/locate_zone\"><span class=\"kw2553\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">locate_zone</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"UTC\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-member\">\n<h2 id=\"std::chrono::zoned_traits.3Cconst_std::chrono::time_zone.2A.3E::locate_zone\"><span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::chrono::zoned_traits&lt;const std::chrono::time_zone*&gt;::</span>locate_zone</h2>\n<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">static</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/time_zone\"><span class=\"kw2595\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">time_zone</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> locate_zone<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view\"><span class=\"kw1256\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string_view</span></span></a> name<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns the time zone pointer for the time zone designated by <code>name</code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value_2\">Return value </h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/locate_zone\"><span class=\"kw2553\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">locate_zone</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>name<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Member functions","id":"Member_functions"},{"depth":2,"text":"std::chrono::zoned_traits<const std::chrono::time_zone*>::default_zone","id":"std::chrono::zoned_traits.3Cconst_std::chrono::time_zone.2A.3E::default_zone"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":2,"text":"std::chrono::zoned_traits<const std::chrono::time_zone*>::locate_zone","id":"std::chrono::zoned_traits.3Cconst_std::chrono::time_zone.2A.3E::locate_zone"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value_2"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"chrono","title":"Date and time utilities"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::chrono::zoned_traits","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++20. The class zoned_traits provides a way to customize the behavior of the constructors of std::chrono::zoned_time with…"},{"label":"Member functions"},{"label":"std::chrono::zoned_traits<const std::chrono::time_zone*>::d…","note":"Returns a time zone pointer for the default time zone (UTC).","children":[{"label":"Return value","note":"std::chrono::locate_zone(\"UTC\")."}]},{"label":"std::chrono::zoned_traits<const std::chrono::time_zone*>::l…","note":"Returns the time zone pointer for the time zone designated by name.","children":[{"label":"Return value","note":"std::chrono::locate_zone(name)."}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":161,"codeBlockCount":0}
